From e84abb808954f2b91298bbd4ece668e4d229afcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:14:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 47/65] llama/server: per-step host costs of the spec loop off
 the critical path

- llama_kv_cache::seq_rm of one sequence walks the sequence's (pos, cell) index instead of all n_ctx cells: the rollback
  after verify (target) and the draft-region removal (MTP context) each scanned 204800 cells per step
  [LLAMA_KV_SEQ_RM_SCAN=1: the scan]
- KQ mask of a ubatch of one sequence that owns every used cell: one vectorizable pass over the cell positions plus the
  cells at the ubatch's positions from the sequence index; same values [LLAMA_KV_MASK_FAST=0: the generic loop]
- server: the context tokens are copied into the draft params every step only for the n-gram drafters
  (common_speculative_needs_prompt)

Host time per step (Qwen, -np 1, ctx 204800, MTP n=4): rollback + process_token 236 -> 6 us, draft-region removal +
batch build 119 -> 2 us; at 89k context also verify launch 305 -> 139 us (mask) and draft setup 82 -> 4 us (prompt copy).
Greedy md5 (plain + MTP) equal to 575e3d893.
